  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Luis Arraez broke Atlanta open with a two-run single in the ninth, capping a four-RBI night that turned a narrow lead into a final margin.",
    "what_this_means": "The game was decided early. Whisenhunt gave them five clean innings and they built a four-run lead by the second inning, then spent six innings protecting it. This is the grind they know. Pitching holds, offense doesn't need to do much, and the bullpen preserves what was built. Arraez made that formula work by driving in all four runs across two separate moments. The ninth-inning single turned a 5-2 game into a cushion they didn't have to hold their breath on. That's what separates a win that feels managed from one that slips away. Three straight wins on a roster that sits 16.5 games back only works if this kind of production holds.",
